    "target_text": "Locate the two red (2) endpoints. Traverse the rounded DDA line between them using max(abs(row delta), abs(column delta)) steps; on that path map zero to red (2) and blue (1) to green (3), preserving every cell off the path.",
    "target_status": "verified_semantic_rule",
    "source": "canonical written solution and executable program",
    "solution_steps": [
      "Find the two red (2) endpoint coordinates in row-major order.",
      "Set the DDA step count to the larger absolute endpoint-axis difference.",
      "For every integer step from zero through that count, interpolate both coordinates and round each to the nearest integer using ties-to-even.",
      "At each visited coordinate, change zero to red (2) and blue (1) to green (3).",
      "Preserve both endpoints and every cell outside the visited DDA coordinates."
    ],
